{"lines": ["Nineteen forty-four. Something is gassing people through their windows. And you? You left yours open.", "Mattoon, Illinois. One night, Aline Kearney smells something sickly sweet.", "Then her legs go numb.", "She blames the flowers. So would you, mid-scroll.", "After midnight, Bert Kearney sees a tall man in a tight cap at her window.", "He chases him. The man vanishes.", "The paper shouts: Anesthetic Prowler on Loose. Soon, over two dozen report gassings.", "One woman finds a damp cloth on her porch, sniffs it, and gets violently sick.", "Of course. You'd sniff it too. You sniff expired milk.", "Lab tests find nothing on it.", "The town panics, like your group chat after someone types, we need to talk.", "Armed patrols roam. A woman loading a shotgun blasts a hole in her kitchen wall.", "Honestly? That's how you'd go out.", "Then one attack turns out to be spilled nail polish.", "Police decide there was probably no gasser. Just fear, spreading house to house.", "The attacks stop. Nobody is ever caught.", "But Bert swore a man stood at that window. So who was it?", "Real gasser, or a town that scared itself sick? Comment below. And close your window. You'd sniff the cloth."], "words": [["Nineteen", 0.0, 0.235], ["forty-four.", 0.235, 0.5], ["Something", 1.12, 1.52], ["is", 1.52, 1.7], ["gassing", 1.7, 2.02], ["people", 2.02, 2.3], ["through", 2.3, 2.6], ["their", 2.6, 2.74], ["windows.", 2.74, 2.96], ["And", 3.54, 3.62], ["you?", 3.62, 3.86], ["You", 4.1, 4.24], ["left", 4.24, 4.4], ["yours", 4.4, 4.64], ["open.", 4.64, 5.06], ["Mattoon,", 6.009, 6.3], ["Illinois.", 6.46, 6.64], ["One", 7.14, 7.18], ["night,", 7.18, 7.42], ["Aline", 7.72, 8.003], ["Kearney", 8.003, 8.4], ["smells", 8.4, 8.64], ["something", 8.64, 9.12], ["sickly", 9.12, 9.54], ["sweet.", 9.54, 9.76], ["Then", 10.682, 10.82], ["her", 10.82, 10.98], ["legs", 10.98, 11.2], ["go", 11.2, 11.52], ["numb.", 11.52, 11.78], ["She", 12.82, 12.94], ["blames", 12.94, 13.14], ["the", 13.14, 13.42], [